                <pb facs="0438" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg380"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 2.</seg></opener>
                <head>The Mexican empire.</head>
                <p>The following telegram from the emperor Maximilian was handed to the Patrie
                    yesterday by the Mexican legation:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">[Valentia, October 9—1 o’clock a. m. ]</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapultepec</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">September</hi> 27.</p>
                <p>To General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Almonte</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Paris</hi>:</p>
                <p>You will inform the legations that excellent spirits prevail among all classes.
                    The cabinet is formed at last. We are on the best terms with our allies. The
                    railway is open to Apizaco.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MAXIMILIAN,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
